mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course is consist of several teaching modules, including <em>brain structure and function</em>, <em>brain disorders</em>, and <em>cutting-edge technologies in brain science</em>. The lectures will be given by the active researchers and instructors at the forefront of brain science research. Adopting a thematic seminar format, each lecturer will present recent research achievements in brain science， and summarize state-of-the-art advances spanning fundamental brain research to clinical translation. The course aims to guide undergraduate students to gain an accessible and comprehensive understanding of the latest research progress in brain science.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
